{
  "schema_version": "2.0",
  "id": "16879_ageru",
  "headword": "{揚|あ}げる",
  "reading": "あげる",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to deep-fry",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to deep-fry",
      "explanation": "To cook food by submerging it in hot oil. Written with the kanji {揚|あ} to distinguish from other verbs read あげる."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "16879_ageru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{鶏肉|とりにく}をカラッと{揚|あ}げる。",
      "english": "I deep-fry the chicken until crispy.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "16879_ageru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{天|てん}ぷらは{高温|こうおん}の{油|あぶら}で{揚|あ}げるのがコツだ。",
      "english": "The trick to tempura is frying it in high-temperature oil.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "16879_ageru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{母|はは}が{揚|あ}げたコロッケは{外|そと}はサクサク、{中|なか}はふわふわだ。",
      "english": "The croquettes my mother deep-fried are crispy on the outside and fluffy on the inside.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "USAGE:\nThis kanji ({揚|あ}げる) specifically indicates deep-frying. Other あげる verbs use different kanji: {上|あ}げる (to raise), {挙|あ}げる (to cite), {掲|あ}げる (to display). The intransitive counterpart is {揚|あ}がる.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {油|あぶら}で{揚|あ}げる (to fry in oil)\n- カラッと{揚|あ}げる (to fry until crispy)\n- {素揚|すあ}げ (deep-frying without batter)",
